      "role": "user",
      "content": "that's a really intense way to put it... \"paves the way for passive compliance.\" so you're saying it's not just catchy branding, but that these phrases are actually structured to function like linguistic shortcuts that skip the part of the brain that analyzes whether a product is actually useful? if that's the case, how deep does this go? are there certain word combinations that act as stronger \"triggers\" than others to make people stop questioning things?",
